\hypertarget{justification-of-tools}{%
\section{Justification of Tools:}\label{justification-of-tools}}

Python\textquotesingle s NumPy library was used for basic numerical
computation. The derivations rely on the principles of
Bayes\textquotesingle{} Rule and the property of conjugate priors. Since
the problem involves estimating the scale parameter (\(\theta\)) of a
Gamma distribution, the analytical solution requires the conjugate prior
to be an Inverse Gamma distribution, whose functional form defines the
structure of the resulting posterior. The formulas for the mean and mode
of the Inverse Gamma distribution determine the final Bayes point
estimates.

